---
title: Checkout user flow, from POST to completion
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant C as Client
  participant O as Orchestrator
  participant I as Inventory
  participant R as Order Service
  participant P as Payment Service
  participant G as Gateway
  C->>O: POST /v1/checkouts (cart + key)
  O->>I: reserve stock (HTTP)
  I-->>O: RESERVED + trusted prices
  Note over O: ONE transaction: saga + order.create in outbox
  O-->>C: 202 order_id (RUNNING)
  O->>R: order.create
  R-->>O: reply Succeeded (order PENDING_PAYMENT)
  O->>P: payment.initiate
  P->>G: create gateway order
  G-->>P: order id, awaiting payment
  Note over G,P: customer pays, webhook or polling tells the payment service (lost reply: UNKNOWN, found by lookup)
  alt payment succeeded
    P-->>O: reply Succeeded
    O->>R: order.mark-paid
    R-->>O: order PAID
    O->>I: inventory.confirm
    I-->>O: stock consumed
    Note over O: saga COMPLETED
  else payment failed or expired
    P-->>O: reply Failed
    O->>R: order.cancel
    O->>I: inventory.release
    Note over O: saga COMPENSATED
  end
  C->>O: GET /v1/checkouts/id
  O-->>C: status, current step, steps
  Note over O,I: before payment a step that cannot complete compensates by itself (order cancelled, stock released). After payment a step that cannot finish leaves the saga STUCK; a person can fix it (admin revive), and after 10 minutes the saga refunds the payment, cancels the paid order and restocks by itself. A crash before the saga transaction is cleaned up by the sweeper, which closes the attempt first
